  "notes": "The research calls this \"the most harmonically explicit corner of the ringtone lane\" and gives the reason — the vocal is sung, not chanted — so this is the one entry on the axis that turns `chords.impliedByRiff` **off**. There is a pad, it states changes, and the changes are the ones the research names: `i–VI–III–VII` leads, `I–V–vi–IV` is the major-key sung form it names beside it, and `harmonicRhythm` moves to `1_per_bar` first where the rest of this lane vamps. `session.scales` carries `major` at weight 3 for the same reason. The lead is the Auto-Tuned vocal treated as a synth — \"quantised pitch, stepwise motion, wide leaps landing on chord tones\" — which is `chordToneBias` 0.9, `intervals.step` 0.62, `octaveJumpProb` up to 0.2 and `structure` `question_answer`, with `timbreHint` `pitched_vocal_chop`. ⛔ **The pre-hook lift is a real section, not a density change.** `arrangement` uses `prechorus`, which the engine knows, with its own 4-bar block and its own rule; no other entry in this batch has one. ⚠ **Confidence is medium and the research says why**: the self-production credit and the era are sourced, and \"harmonic detail inferred from the sung-hook format\" — so the four progression families are a reading of the format rather than a transcription, and `session.bpm` 140–160 comes from a band marked [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ **The 120–128 straight dance crossovers are not in this file.** The archetype already carries a `crossover` mode pinned at 128, and this model does not author `modes`, so it inherits that one rather than restating it — an artist authoring its own modes replaces its genre's, and replacing four with a duplicate would have cost the other three. ⚠ The synth bass doubling the 808 on hooks is **not expressible**: `bass808.role` stays `bassline` here, so the separate bass generator returns nothing and a `bassline` block would be authored dead. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
